<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rastafari</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rastafari movement</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rastafari is a religious and cultural movement that emerged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> in the 1930s. It regards Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haile-selassie">Haile Selassie</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> as a messianic figure. The movement extended the symbolic influence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a> into global popular culture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rastafari.jpg" alt="Rastafari" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oren neu dag · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ethiopia_(1897%E2%80%931974).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
